        "articleTitle": "ISO structure and related activities [automobile electronics diagnostics]",
        "volume": null,
        "issue": null,
        "startPage": "3/1",
        "endPage": "313",
        "publisher": "IET",
        "articleContentType": "Conferences",
        "publicationTitle": "IEE Communication Standards for European On-Board-Diagnostics Seminar (Ref. No. 1998/294)",
        "authors": [],
        "abstract": "The permanent desire for greater safety, driving comfort, and environmental compatibility is leading to a rapid increase in electronic control units and sensors in vehicles. Added functions and the corresponding equipment create even not only a bewildering tangle of cables, but also a considerable confusion of functional connections. It becomes more and more difficult to diagnose faults in such systems, and solve them within a reasonable period. In such a frustrating situation the International Standards Organisation (ISO) is ready and prepared to help in preparing standards to facilitate diagnostic applications world-wide. The author gives an idea and impression of the role of ISO and their national member bodies in developing vehicle electronics diagnostic standards for everyone's use: the manufacturer, the consumer, the legislator, the surveillance agencies, the workshop etc.",
